    >[-] Design a minimal headless ParticleOS fork/profile as the alternative OS candidate =mini-server-particleos-profile $Initial local fork created at ~/Products/personal-os, branch personal-os from upstream e55d7a95e3b9da8a2291ca17b7327b204f2c5a56; dotfiles submodule pinned to c84190f5aaa1f63e542ffff5f198ce3de75899c0. README/AGENTS, canonical charter/history and retained bootc reference migrated here. Default mini-server overlay selects stable Fedora 44 early enough to load correct distro fragments; mkosi summary parses, no image built. Next implement trimmed account/root/home/security policy, committed dotfiles staging without build-side chezmoi, and safe target-side first-boot/apply with retries, revision tracking, edit preservation and dependent-service gating. Reuse actual target chezmoi guards; narrow paru hook to Arch. Resolve production signing/recovery and artifact publishing separately; no origin/GitHub fork/push/install yet. Keep bootc evidence as fallback until new candidate passes equivalent VM tests.$ ^2026-10-02T18:01 #01a0ff47-9cfc-76f6-9c64-24a6d8d4ce77
