real visudo and adapted offline unit verification. No real account commands, image build, SELinux/SSH/console or VM pass. Installer credential handoff, chezmoi apply/update lifecycle, secret readiness and runtime dependent-service stopping remain incomplete; enrollment never creates the workload-ready marker. Source lifecycle child prototype now exists but is not automatically invoked. Runtime-only root-owned account context selects the intended target user. Factory policy permits only OS-recorded ancestor pins, not implicit rollback or unrelated sources. Conservative three-way source promotion preserves edits/untracked files/Git metadata; private journal/lock and per-file retries; generated-config conflicts retain a private candidate. Native init/apply uses real target context and immutable guards, with less-interactive/error-on-conflict and force disabled. Applied revision/context recorded only after success; same pin/context not blindly reapplied. Sixty-two offline tests pass, all lifecycle init/apply and workload probes mocked; no actual target apply/image/SELinux/VM pass. Child requires workloads already stopped and readiness absent but does not stop them or create readiness. Next root-side automatic controller, runtime failure/stop handling, binary/private-listener/secret gates, then inherited-policy review and isolated VM validation. Keep action in progress and automatic application disabled; no push or production change.$ ^2026-10-02T18:27 #01a0ff5f-393d-72d4-a01e-ab236e05ebc4
